  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Pre-Health Occupations A.S. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published July 30, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7739/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 60.5-65; this seed models the path that satisfies the map's fixed Semester 3 (17 units) and Semester 4 (15 units) headers = 15.5 + 15 + 17 + 15 = 62.5 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; AH 108 at 0.5 units, the low end of the 0.5-2 range). PATH SELECTION (documented): the map offers interdependent paths — (CHEM 305 & CHEM 306) OR CHEM 309, and (BIOL 430 & BIOL 431) OR BIOL 302. The fixed Sem 3 (17) header requires BIOL 431 (5 units), which requires BIOL 430 (Sem 2); the fixed Sem 4 (15) header requires CHEM 306 (5 units), which requires CHEM 305 (Sem 1). Therefore the printed path uses CHEM 305/306 and BIOL 430/431. If CHEM 309 is taken, Sem 4 CHEM 306 becomes an elective; if BIOL 302 is taken, Sem 3 BIOL 431 becomes an elective (and up to 3-4 additional elective units may be needed per the map note). Choice slots: (1) GE STAT C1000 / * C1000H, Area 2 — STAT C1000 selected; (2) ME AH 108 / DAST 100 / DHYG 100 / OTA 100 / PTA 100 Introduction to Health Occupations (0.5-2) — AH 108 selected (first-listed) at 0.5 units; (3) GE ENGL C1000 / ** 488 / H+ ESLW 340 +, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (4) ME CHEM 305 / + 309 (5), Areas 5A/5C — CHEM 305 selected (first-listed; the CHEM 305 & 306 path); (5) ME BIOL 430 / + 302 Anatomy and Physiology (3-5) — BIOL 430 selected at 5 units (the BIOL 430 & 431 path); (6) ME NUTRI 300 / 480 H Nutrition (3) — NUTRI 300 selected; (7) ME ANTH 310 / 481 / H SOC 300 / 321 / 482 H (3) — ANTH 310 selected (first-listed); (8) ME COMM C1000 / 481 H Introduction to Public Speaking (3), Area 1C — COMM C1000 selected. Documented prerequisites (all satisfied in-plan): CHEM 305/309 require Elementary Algebra; BIOL 430 requires CHEM 305, 309, or 400 (CHEM 305 in plan); BIOL 431 requires BIOL 430 (in plan); CHEM 306 requires CHEM 305 (in plan); BIOL 440 requires CHEM 305, 309, or 400 (in plan). Students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo; students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. Department Notes (documented): Northern CA Nursing Programs require CHEM 305; Southern CA Nursing Programs require CHEM 309. Pre-Nursing students may apply for an AS in Nutrition (CSU Path) via CHEM 305/309/400, NUTRI 300, STAT 300, PSYC 300, BIOL 440 — see the Nutrition Department. ETHNS 300 fills Cal-GETC Area 6. EDUC 300 fills Cal-GETC Area 4. BIOL 440 fills Cal-GETC Area 5B. PSYC C1000 fills Cal-GETC Area 4. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499 (see a counselor to verify elective units needed). Health & Health Profession Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
